      "kernel_class": "attention_decode",
      "regime": "decode",
      "key": "deciding whether a KV-streaming / double-buffer rewrite can pay on an already-tuned decode attention kernel, gfx950/CDNA4",
      "lifecycle": "active",
      "layer": "learned",
      "levers": [
        "mem.double-buffer",
        "diag.counters"
      ],
      "cost": "L3",
      "type": "anti-pattern",
      "confidence": "★",
      "effect": "~1.00x, no patch survived: a ground-up double-buffered streaming rewrite of the large-ctx decode case returned nothing, and the arithmetic ceiling for that case alone was ~1.09x geomean even under a dream near-peak-bandwidth assumption",
      "roofline": "apparent ~0.5 of achievable HBM roof, actually VALU+LDS bound with VALU:VMEM issue ratio ~34:1 and LDS-wait above busy cycles",
      "verified_on": "2026-08-12",
      "last_seen": "2026-08-12",
      "attempts": 1,
      "confirms_blind": 0,
      "confirms_cited": 0,
      "losses": 0,
      "title": "Classify with counters, not with the fraction-of-roof number, before a streaming rewrite",
      "lever": "Read the VALU:VMEM issue ratio and the LDS-wait-vs-busy split first, and confirm the loads are EXPOSED on the critical path; a fraction-of-roof figure that looks like headroom can be a compute-tail artifact (memory idle during dequant, LDS transpose and the softmax tail).",
      "apply": "Also bound the axis by register footprint: when both operand tiles already fit inside the occupancy footprint, the loads are front-loaded and in flight, so a second buffer has nothing to overlap and the whole prefetch family is closed for that shape.",
      "verify": "Compute the best-case ceiling for the one case the rewrite targets and weight it into the geomean before committing a deep round; if the dream number is a couple of percent overall, spend the round on another axis.",
      "pitfall": "A fraction-of-roof reading was taken as bandwidth headroom and funded a full streaming rewrite -> the memory system was idle during the compute tail, not saturated -> counters (VALU:VMEM, LDS-wait) reclassified the kernel and the rewrite was abandoned with no patch.",
      "caution": "Also verify where the remaining VALU actually goes before declaring the compute side closed: here a byte-gather LDS transpose was a large share of it, which is a different (and still open) lever from streaming.",
      "source": "run paged_attention_decode-ch16h, 16h time-scaling campaign, 2026-08-12"
    }
  ]
